    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d974">

                <pb facs="0924" n="912" xml:id="pg912"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/72: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-12T20:00:00+01:00">November 12,
                            1943—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7894. For Alling from Hoskins. General Crain cabling War Department today that
                    British War Office advise they have not as yet made any deliveries of military
                    equipment to Saudi Arabia and have agreed not to make any deliveries pending
                    further discussions and agreement with us. Their main concern remains that no
                    excessive quantities be furnished. [Hoskins.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
